      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/unusual_ornamental_fish_bred_in_indonesia_3_leporinus_affinis_en/",
      "html": "<p>This is another very attractive large tetra relative, currently offered as bred specimens from Indonesia. This Leporinus attains a maximum length of about 25 cm total length and stays a bit smaller than the otherwise very similar L. fasciatus, which reaches about 30 cm total length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/unusual_ornamental_fish_bred_in_indonesia_3_leporinus_affinis_en/",
      "html": "<p>It is almost impossible to keep it in a planted tank. So it is best to keep this type of banded Leporinus in very large tanks along with other large tetras, cichlids and catfish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/unusual_ornamental_fish_bred_in_indonesia_3_leporinus_affinis_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species needs a lot of plant material as food.</p>"
    }
